From fe45cc6af75a70af8bb47a1ce1b7d01ff1e7ff9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:56:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Encrypt clipboard history with a Keystore-backed key

Clipboard text is stored as AES-256-GCM ciphertext. The data keys are wrapped by
a non-exportable master key in the Android Keystore (StrongBox when available,
otherwise TEE). Duplicates are found with a keyed HMAC instead of the plaintext.

Database version 5 adds the encrypted and textHash columns. Rows written by
older versions are encrypted on startup, rows that can no longer be decrypted
(lost keys) are dropped.
